# <%= gem_name %>

The <%= theme_title %> theme for [Avo](https://avohq.io).

<!-- Add a screenshot of the theme here. -->

## Installation

Add the gem to your app's `Gemfile` and run `bundle install`:

```ruby
gem "<%= gem_name %>"
```

While developing the theme, point the Gemfile at your checkout instead:

```ruby
gem "<%= gem_name %>", path: "<%= gem_relative_root %>"
```

Restart the server, open the appearance picker, and choose "<%= theme_title %>". To make
it the default, or to limit which themes the picker offers, set `theme` / `themes`
under `config.appearance` in `config/initializers/avo.rb`.

## Layout

| Path                                                   | Purpose                                                   |
| ------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| `lib/avo/<%= theme_id %>_theme/theme.rb`               | The manifest: `Avo::<%= gem_module_name %>::Theme`        |
| `app/assets/stylesheets/avo/themes/<%= theme_id %>.css` | The look: tokens scoped to `.avo-theme-<%= theme_id %>`  |
| `app/views/avo/themes/<%= theme_id %>/`                | Optional partial overrides, mirroring Avo's `app/views`   |
| `app/assets/images/avo/themes/<%= theme_id %>/`        | Optional logo, favicon, placeholder, backgrounds, fonts   |

To override a partial, copy it from Avo into the views directory above with the
same relative path, for example `app/views/avo/themes/<%= theme_id %>/avo/partials/_logo.html.erb`.

## Publishing

1. Fill in the author, email, homepage, and license in `<%= gem_name %>.gemspec`, and
   credit any reused palette or artwork in `NOTICE`.
2. Build and push:

```bash
gem build <%= gem_name %>.gemspec
gem push <%= gem_name %>-0.1.0.gem
```

Bump `Avo::<%= gem_module_name %>::VERSION` in `lib/avo/<%= theme_id %>_theme/version.rb` before each release.
